1
00:00:01,520 --> 00:00:03,650
Wealth, fame, power...

2
00:00:03,650 --> 00:00:07,820
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,
obtained everything the world has to offer.

3
00:00:07,820 --> 00:00:11,660
What he said in his final moments
drove countless souls to the seas.

4
00:00:11,660 --> 00:00:13,660
You want my treasure?

5
00:00:13,660 --> 00:00:15,450
Go ahead.

6
00:00:15,450 --> 00:00:16,660
Find it!

7
00:00:16,660 --> 00:00:19,250
Everything is right where I left it!

8
00:00:21,670 --> 00:00:26,380
People set their sights on the Grand Line
in pursuit of their dreams.

9
00:00:26,380 --> 00:00:29,630
The world has truly entered
the Great Pirate Era!

10
00:01:50,310 --> 00:01:54,130
Those three think they can
mock me! Screw that!

11
00:01:54,130 --> 00:01:57,970
I'm considering this
a formal declaration of war.

12
00:01:58,680 --> 00:02:01,200
Perfect timing, Mohji!

13
00:02:01,850 --> 00:02:06,230
"Beast Tamer" Mohji
First Mate, Buggy Pirates

14
00:02:02,760 --> 00:02:04,700
Would you mind

15
00:02:04,700 --> 00:02:06,270
if I took Roronoa Zoro's head?

16
00:02:07,960 --> 00:02:09,330
Be my guest!

17
00:02:21,330 --> 00:02:27,630
Treasure

18
00:02:27,580 --> 00:02:29,960
What's with that dog?

19
00:02:31,070 --> 00:02:32,380
A dog!

20
00:02:40,290 --> 00:02:43,190
Hey, Zoro! It's not moving at all!

21
00:02:43,190 --> 00:02:45,970
Hell if I care! It can
do whatever it wants!

22
00:02:46,930 --> 00:02:48,440
Think it's dead?

23
00:02:54,690 --> 00:02:58,110
Ow! Ow! Ow!

24
00:02:58,110 --> 00:03:02,450
Ow! What's the big deal,
you stupid dog?!

25
00:03:02,450 --> 00:03:06,090
Would you stop messing around
at a time like this?!

26
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:09,880
Damn dog!

27
00:03:10,960 --> 00:03:12,670
Not enough blood...

28
00:03:17,340 --> 00:03:19,300
Hey, Navigator!

29
00:03:20,260 --> 00:03:23,720
I guess you can have this
since you did save me!

30
00:03:25,390 --> 00:03:27,810
Oh! The key to the cage!

31
00:03:27,810 --> 00:03:30,350
You went and got it for me?!

32
00:03:30,350 --> 00:03:32,400
Now we're even.

33
00:03:33,860 --> 00:03:36,270
I'm saved!

34
00:03:46,450 --> 00:03:48,960
Stupid dog! Stupid dog!

35
00:03:48,960 --> 00:03:52,210
That's not food!
Gimme back that key!

36
00:03:55,620 --> 00:03:57,720
Gimme! Gimme! Gimme!

37
00:03:57,720 --> 00:03:59,170
Stop that!

38
00:04:00,170 --> 00:04:03,130
Quit bullying Chouchou,
you delinquents!

39
00:04:04,620 --> 00:04:05,720
Chouchou?

40
00:04:06,600 --> 00:04:08,060
Who are you, old-timer?

41
00:04:08,060 --> 00:04:10,810
I'm this town's mayor!

42
00:04:08,140 --> 00:04:14,070
Boodle
Harbor Village Mayor

43
00:04:10,810 --> 00:04:13,510
Who are you?!

44
00:04:13,510 --> 00:04:14,060
Huh?

45
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:22,960
How's Zoro?!

46
00:04:22,960 --> 00:04:25,300
He needs to see a doctor,

47
00:04:25,300 --> 00:04:28,200
but he said he'd sleep it off
and went to bed.

48
00:04:34,940 --> 00:04:37,420
So this dog's name is Chouchou?

49
00:04:38,540 --> 00:04:41,170
What's he just sitting here for?

50
00:04:41,770 --> 00:04:43,090
He's guarding the shop.

51
00:04:43,610 --> 00:04:47,960
Oh! This is a... pet food shop?

52
00:04:47,960 --> 00:04:53,520
Yes. A good friend of mine
owned this shop.

53
00:04:57,890 --> 00:04:58,780
There you go.

54
00:05:01,650 --> 00:05:06,240
I'm just here to feed
his dog in his place.

55
00:05:07,170 --> 00:05:08,040
"In his place"?

56
00:05:08,040 --> 00:05:09,130
Yes.

57
00:05:09,130 --> 00:05:14,480
He got sick and passed away,
oh, three months ago.

58
00:05:14,480 --> 00:05:18,960
You mean to tell us he's been waiting
here for his master all this time?

59
00:05:21,700 --> 00:05:23,380
That's the general consensus...

60
00:05:28,930 --> 00:05:32,770
but I don't think that's the case.

61
00:05:33,200 --> 00:05:35,160
Chouchou is a smart dog.

62
00:05:35,160 --> 00:05:39,070
He's probably long since realized
that his master passed on.

63
00:05:43,550 --> 00:05:46,030
Then why is he guarding the shop?

64
00:05:46,560 --> 00:05:50,030
I believe it's because Chouchou
regards this shop as his treasure.

65
00:05:50,810 --> 00:05:56,330
I think he continues to protects it
in memory of his loving master.

66
00:05:56,330 --> 00:05:59,430
I've tried to get him somewhere
safer on many occasions,

67
00:05:59,430 --> 00:06:03,300
but he won't take as much
as a step away from here.

68
00:06:26,650 --> 00:06:28,210
Huh? What are those roars?!

69
00:06:28,210 --> 00:06:31,120
It's him! Beast Tamer Mohji!

70
00:06:32,160 --> 00:06:34,420
What do you mean by
"Beast Tamer"?!

71
00:06:34,420 --> 00:06:36,160
W-Wait! Hold on!

72
00:06:40,840 --> 00:06:42,970
C'mon, something's on its way.

73
00:06:42,970 --> 00:06:44,420
Gimme back the key.

74
00:06:49,220 --> 00:06:51,870
Oh, I see your friends
have deserted you.

75
00:06:51,870 --> 00:06:53,640
And you only just escaped...

76
00:06:54,380 --> 00:06:55,430
Who are you?

77
00:06:55,980 --> 00:06:59,850
I am Beast Tamer Mohji,
a member of the Buggy Pirates.

78
00:07:01,460 --> 00:07:04,480
That sure is a weird
animal suit you got on!

79
00:07:07,110 --> 00:07:09,780
How rude! This is my hair!

80
00:07:09,780 --> 00:07:11,610
That's even weirder!

81
00:07:11,610 --> 00:07:15,910
Do you think you can rest easy
because you're inside that cage?

82
00:07:15,910 --> 00:07:18,160
You must not know my terrifying skill!

83
00:07:18,160 --> 00:07:23,130
There is no animal in this world that
Beast Tamer Mohji can't tame!

84
00:07:24,120 --> 00:07:24,750
Shake!

85
00:07:27,050 --> 00:07:29,050
Ouch! Ouch! Ouch!

86
00:07:29,050 --> 00:07:29,090
Ouch! Ouch! Ouch!

87
00:07:29,090 --> 00:07:29,130
Ouch! Ouch! Ouch!

88
00:07:29,130 --> 00:07:29,170
Ouch! Ouch! Ouch!

89
00:07:29,170 --> 00:07:29,220
Ouch! Ouch! Ouch!

90
00:07:29,220 --> 00:07:29,260
Ouch! Ouch! Ouch!

91
00:07:29,260 --> 00:07:29,300
Ouch! Ouch! Ouch!

92
00:07:29,300 --> 00:07:29,340
Ouch! Ouch! Ouch!

93
00:07:29,340 --> 00:07:29,380
Ouch! Ouch! Ouch!

94
00:07:29,380 --> 00:07:29,420
Ouch! Ouch! Ouch!

95
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:32,990
You're just some nameless thief.

96
00:07:32,990 --> 00:07:36,470
I couldn't care less if you live or die.
Tell me where Roronoa Zoro is!

97
00:07:37,070 --> 00:07:37,970
No!

98
00:07:38,630 --> 00:07:39,930
Sic him, Richie!

99
00:07:42,690 --> 00:07:45,520
Alright! The cage is open!

100
00:07:51,680 --> 00:07:52,820
An instant death.

101
00:07:53,370 --> 00:07:54,810
Good boy, Richie.

102
00:07:54,810 --> 00:07:58,740
Now let's find Zoro and defeat him
to bolster my reputation.

103
00:08:00,270 --> 00:08:01,380
What is it?

104
00:08:01,380 --> 00:08:03,280
Ah, a pet food store.

105
00:08:03,280 --> 00:08:04,960
Fine, make your meal quick!

106
00:08:07,500 --> 00:08:08,590
What the...?

107
00:08:08,590 --> 00:08:13,300
Is this mutt really trying to keep us
out of this pathetic little shop?

108
00:08:19,230 --> 00:08:21,730
Phew, what a shock!

109
00:08:21,730 --> 00:08:23,730
But at least I'm out of the cage.

110
00:08:26,110 --> 00:08:27,450
Alright!

111
00:08:27,450 --> 00:08:31,990
Now I can kick some butt and get
that thief Nami to be our navigator!

112
00:08:33,240 --> 00:08:34,820
How did you survive that?!

113
00:08:34,820 --> 00:08:36,500
You're alive!

114
00:08:36,500 --> 00:08:37,660
Is it wrong to be alive?

115
00:08:37,660 --> 00:08:42,280
People don't normally crash through
buildings and walk away from it!

116
00:08:42,280 --> 00:08:43,320
They don't?

117
00:08:43,830 --> 00:08:47,180
Why did you come
to this town in the first place?

118
00:08:47,180 --> 00:08:49,050
Why get mixed up with those pirates?

119
00:08:49,050 --> 00:08:51,340
I've just now decided on our goal.

120
00:08:51,340 --> 00:08:54,010
To get a map to the Grand Line
and find a navigator!

121
00:08:56,840 --> 00:09:00,020
That guy in the animal costume
said he was looking for Zoro!

122
00:09:00,020 --> 00:09:00,810
I gotta find him!

123
00:09:12,510 --> 00:09:18,200
Chouchou. This shop belongs
to the two of us!

124
00:09:22,120 --> 00:09:25,000
This bag is too big
for you, Chouchou!

125
00:09:40,850 --> 00:09:43,270
You don't want
to get hurt, Chouchou!

126
00:09:43,270 --> 00:09:44,770
Just leave it to me!

127
00:09:47,980 --> 00:09:50,980
Bad Chouchou! I told you
not to eat the merchandise!

128
00:09:51,600 --> 00:09:53,030
Now let's chow down!

129
00:10:03,430 --> 00:10:06,370
Oh? So you want to fight...

130
00:10:08,540 --> 00:10:11,600
Chouchou, I'm getting
up there in years now.

131
00:10:11,600 --> 00:10:13,940
I gotta check in to the hospital.

132
00:10:13,940 --> 00:10:17,140
But... I'll surely get better!

133
00:10:17,140 --> 00:10:20,050
Guard the shop well
until I come back!

134
00:10:20,060 --> 00:10:23,020
Hold down the fort!

135
00:10:51,290 --> 00:10:53,680
That tickles, Chouchou!

136
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:03,160
I believe it's because Chouchou
regards this shop as his treasure.

137
00:11:03,710 --> 00:11:09,320
I think he continues to protect it
in memory of his loving master.

138
00:11:33,170 --> 00:11:36,250
Damn it! That dog even bit me!

139
00:11:44,350 --> 00:11:47,010
Wait! I just killed you!

140
00:11:49,560 --> 00:11:51,640
It'll take more than that to kill me!

141
00:11:52,570 --> 00:11:54,770
Crush his head for sure this time!

142
00:11:59,090 --> 00:12:01,070
I won't lose to some lion!

143
00:12:01,990 --> 00:12:03,570
Gum-Gum...

144
00:12:06,990 --> 00:12:08,410
Hammer!

145
00:12:13,460 --> 00:12:15,460
Richie!

146
00:12:18,150 --> 00:12:20,660
Just what the hell are you?!

147
00:12:22,090 --> 00:12:25,390
I ate the Gum-Gum Fruit!

148
00:12:25,940 --> 00:12:29,310
You mean... just like Captain Buggy...

149
00:12:29,310 --> 00:12:31,350
you have devil fruit powers?!

150
00:12:35,400 --> 00:12:39,190
I-I get the picture!
Please accept my humble apology!

151
00:12:40,520 --> 00:12:42,840
It's too late for apologies

152
00:12:42,840 --> 00:12:45,200
'cause that dog's treasure
is gone forever.

153
00:12:48,420 --> 00:12:51,950
And that's why...
it's lights out for you!

154
00:13:13,540 --> 00:13:17,400
Pirates are all the same,
every last one!

155
00:13:18,320 --> 00:13:21,360
They take what people hold dear
without a second thought!

156
00:13:22,020 --> 00:13:24,070
So you survived, pirate!

157
00:13:24,750 --> 00:13:28,770
I figured the lion
would've eaten you for sure!

158
00:13:29,350 --> 00:13:31,910
As a pirate, you'll end up
doing the same thing!

159
00:13:32,740 --> 00:13:35,540
You'll gather a crew
and raid town after town!

160
00:13:35,540 --> 00:13:38,030
I should just kill you
right here instead!

161
00:13:38,030 --> 00:13:40,300
Hey! Stop it, young lady!

162
00:13:40,300 --> 00:13:41,960
As if you could ever kill me.

163
00:13:41,960 --> 00:13:43,560
Let's test that theory!

164
00:13:43,560 --> 00:13:45,900
I said stop! What's with you people?!

165
00:13:59,920 --> 00:14:02,030
This is all I was able to rescue.

166
00:14:02,030 --> 00:14:04,320
That bastard went and ate the rest!

167
00:14:05,230 --> 00:14:10,950
He... fought with that lion.
All for that dog's sake.

168
00:14:14,780 --> 00:14:16,760
You fought good!

169
00:14:16,760 --> 00:14:19,200
I didn't see you in action,
but I can tell!

170
00:14:39,120 --> 00:14:41,810
Yeah! Good luck to you, too!

171
00:14:56,710 --> 00:14:59,040
You were beaten?!

172
00:15:00,150 --> 00:15:02,840
I-I'm very sorry, Captain Buggy!

173
00:15:03,620 --> 00:15:06,840
Mohji! I can't believe
you'd lose to Zoro!

174
00:15:06,840 --> 00:15:10,240
No, it wasn't Zoro!
It was Straw Hat!

175
00:15:10,240 --> 00:15:13,750
What?! You got beat
by the kid in the straw hat?!

176
00:15:13,750 --> 00:15:15,600
He ate the... Gum...

177
00:15:15,600 --> 00:15:18,350
Now I'm pissed!

178
00:15:18,350 --> 00:15:20,660
Ready all the Special Buggy Balls!

179
00:15:20,660 --> 00:15:23,610
I'm gonna blow this
entire town to smithereens!

180
00:15:25,410 --> 00:15:26,400
Sorry for earlier!

181
00:15:27,210 --> 00:15:28,190
Huh?

182
00:15:28,190 --> 00:15:29,860
I didn't mean to yell at you...

183
00:15:30,650 --> 00:15:33,700
It's okay! You've been through a lot!

184
00:15:36,390 --> 00:15:38,410
I don't need the details, though.

185
00:15:38,880 --> 00:15:40,740
I'm so pathetic!

186
00:15:40,740 --> 00:15:43,920
If Chouchou and this youngster
won't back down,

187
00:15:43,920 --> 00:15:48,840
then why am I, as mayor, content
to watch the town get trashed?!

188
00:15:49,350 --> 00:15:50,840
Calm down, Mayor!

189
00:15:51,320 --> 00:15:55,050
Forty years ago, this place
was nothing but wilderness.

190
00:15:55,050 --> 00:15:58,930
We all worked together
to clear the land, make fields,

191
00:15:58,930 --> 00:16:02,270
open stores, and build our town.

192
00:16:02,270 --> 00:16:06,560
This town is a treasure
to me and all its citizens!

193
00:16:06,560 --> 00:16:10,240
I won't let them
have their way with it any longer!

194
00:16:10,630 --> 00:16:14,240
Fire a Special Buggy Ball!
Blow the town away!

195
00:16:25,770 --> 00:16:27,880
Even my own house...

196
00:16:29,380 --> 00:16:30,840
Zoro's sleeping in there!

197
00:16:31,500 --> 00:16:34,180
That young man must be dead...

198
00:16:35,110 --> 00:16:37,180
Hey! Zoro! Are you alive?!

199
00:16:37,710 --> 00:16:40,220
That's a hell of a way
to wake a guy up.

200
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:47,020
Not enough sleep...

201
00:16:47,950 --> 00:16:49,960
And just how did you survive?!

202
00:16:49,960 --> 00:16:51,650
Thank goodness! You're alive!

203
00:16:52,100 --> 00:16:55,490
No more sitting idly by
while they run wild here!

204
00:16:56,060 --> 00:16:57,510
I've had it up to here!

205
00:16:57,510 --> 00:17:03,110
These scumbags have zero right
to trample on these forty years!

206
00:17:04,910 --> 00:17:08,250
I am this town's mayor!

207
00:17:09,660 --> 00:17:12,170
I will protect this town!

208
00:17:14,170 --> 00:17:17,200
Stop! Stop, Mayor!

209
00:17:17,200 --> 00:17:19,640
There are fights
a man can't run away from!

210
00:17:19,640 --> 00:17:21,440
Isn't that right, kiddo?!

211
00:17:21,440 --> 00:17:22,430
Right, old guy!

212
00:17:23,380 --> 00:17:24,650
Don't egg him on!

213
00:17:24,650 --> 00:17:27,310
What's he gonna change
by facing them?! It's reckless!

214
00:17:27,940 --> 00:17:29,270
It's absolutely reckless!

215
00:17:32,840 --> 00:17:35,400
I'm coming for you,
Buggy the Clown!

216
00:17:37,580 --> 00:17:39,640
The mayor was crying...

217
00:17:39,640 --> 00:17:41,920
He was? Not that I could see.

218
00:17:41,920 --> 00:17:44,530
Looks like the party's
getting more exciting!

219
00:17:45,500 --> 00:17:46,840
You said it!

220
00:17:47,370 --> 00:17:49,170
This is no time to be laughing!

221
00:17:50,380 --> 00:17:53,380
It's okay! I like that old guy!

222
00:17:53,380 --> 00:17:54,630
I'd never let him die!

223
00:17:55,190 --> 00:17:57,610
In that case...

224
00:17:57,610 --> 00:18:00,270
You're going too?!
But you're wounded!

225
00:18:00,270 --> 00:18:05,270
Getting thrashed hurts my rep
way more than the gut wound itself.

226
00:18:05,800 --> 00:18:08,190
We're headed for the Grand Line.

227
00:18:08,790 --> 00:18:11,630
So we're gonna swipe
that map back from them!

228
00:18:13,510 --> 00:18:15,620
Join our crew, Nami!

229
00:18:16,850 --> 00:18:19,590
I won't become a pirate.

230
00:18:22,360 --> 00:18:25,830
How about this? We team up
to achieve a common goal!

231
00:18:28,500 --> 00:18:30,750
The second shot is ready, sir!

232
00:18:31,070 --> 00:18:32,210
Alright! Fire!

233
00:18:32,680 --> 00:18:35,710
Get out here, Buggy the Clown!

234
00:18:38,550 --> 00:18:41,400
I am Mayor Boodle!

235
00:18:41,400 --> 00:18:45,730
This town is our treasure, so I'm
going to protect it by taking you out!

236
00:18:45,730 --> 00:18:50,240
What are you, stupid?!
Treasure is gold, silver, and jewels!

237
00:18:50,240 --> 00:18:53,150
This town, a treasure?!
Cut the crap!

238
00:18:53,570 --> 00:18:56,190
You'd never understand how I feel–

239
00:18:57,480 --> 00:19:03,830
Soon, I'll conquer the Grand Line and
flashily obtain all of the world's riches!

240
00:19:03,830 --> 00:19:06,050
The world's riches are mine!

241
00:19:06,050 --> 00:19:09,060
No one else in this world
needs treasure but me!

242
00:19:09,060 --> 00:19:13,290
Since you love this town so much,
shall I level it along with you?

243
00:19:14,250 --> 00:19:16,960
Quit blowing hot air and fight me!

244
00:19:17,740 --> 00:19:18,880
Don't get cocky now!

245
00:19:19,380 --> 00:19:23,600
I won't let you destroy this town
even if it costs me my life!

246
00:19:25,140 --> 00:19:26,180
Fire!

247
00:19:29,130 --> 00:19:30,230
The straw hat guy!

248
00:19:43,150 --> 00:19:46,630
I'm here to kick your ass,
just like I promised!

249
00:20:01,650 --> 00:20:03,010
Straw Hat?!

250
00:20:08,960 --> 00:20:13,320
How dare you just waltz back here...

251
00:20:13,320 --> 00:20:16,290
to Captain Buggy!

252
00:20:16,290 --> 00:20:20,930
Listen! All I want is the map
and the treasure!

253
00:20:20,930 --> 00:20:23,030
Yeah, we know.

254
00:20:23,630 --> 00:20:26,400
Youngsters...
Why'd you come here?!

255
00:20:26,400 --> 00:20:29,790
This isn't your business, so butt out!

256
00:20:30,790 --> 00:20:36,000
This is my fight!
I will protect my town!

257
00:20:38,620 --> 00:20:39,840
Now stop meddling!

258
00:20:48,490 --> 00:20:50,220
What the hell?!

259
00:20:50,780 --> 00:20:53,200
Why did you attack the mayor?!

260
00:20:54,260 --> 00:20:55,190
He was in the way!

261
00:20:56,340 --> 00:20:57,890
Good thinking.

262
00:20:57,890 --> 00:21:00,400
No doubt this geezer
was prepared to die.

263
00:21:01,370 --> 00:21:02,690
This is for the best.

264
00:21:02,690 --> 00:21:04,500
But this is going overboard!

265
00:21:04,500 --> 00:21:07,540
There were plenty of other ways
you could've done it!

266
00:21:13,710 --> 00:21:17,330
Hey, Big Nose!

267
00:21:18,760 --> 00:21:20,880
That's the one thing
you shouldn't say!

268
00:21:21,510 --> 00:21:24,770
You're dead meat,
you flashy mongrel!

269
00:21:24,770 --> 00:21:27,050
How dare you...

270
00:21:27,050 --> 00:21:29,430
Flashily fire the Buggy Ball!

271
00:21:30,510 --> 00:21:33,070
Why'd you say that, you idiot!

272
00:21:33,070 --> 00:21:34,740
Hey, Luffy! Run!

273
00:21:34,740 --> 00:21:35,730
That...

274
00:21:35,730 --> 00:21:37,100
Time to blow up!

275
00:21:37,700 --> 00:21:39,610
...won't work on me!

276
00:21:40,940 --> 00:21:42,480
Gum-Gum...

277
00:21:43,860 --> 00:21:46,110
Balloon!

278
00:21:47,890 --> 00:21:49,340
What is that guy?!

279
00:21:49,340 --> 00:21:50,780
But the Buggy Ball will...

280
00:21:53,730 --> 00:21:55,330
He bounced it back!

281
00:21:55,330 --> 00:21:57,290
Give us a heads up first, will ya?!

282
00:22:06,140 --> 00:22:07,930
Alright! Fewer enemies now!

283
00:22:07,930 --> 00:22:10,000
Really, what are you?!

284
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:11,760
You had me there for a sec.

285
00:22:20,120 --> 00:22:23,570
Ever since fighting that lion,
I knew you weren't quite normal!

286
00:22:23,570 --> 00:22:27,240
No human can do that!
Explain yourself!

287
00:22:27,240 --> 00:22:30,570
What was that balloon-inflating
thing you just did?!

288
00:22:31,050 --> 00:22:32,820
That's Gum-Gum Balloon!

289
00:22:32,820 --> 00:22:35,040
And how did you do that?!

290
00:22:35,600 --> 00:22:37,200
What are you, a monster?!

291
00:22:39,130 --> 00:22:42,710
How dare you flashily try
to do me in...

292
00:22:48,100 --> 00:22:50,510
He used his henchmen as shields!

293
00:22:59,380 --> 00:23:01,250
What happened here?!

294
00:23:03,280 --> 00:23:04,900
You!

295
00:23:05,490 --> 00:23:06,030
Hey!

296
00:23:07,050 --> 00:23:08,720
The straw hat guy!

297
00:23:08,720 --> 00:23:11,010
C-C-Captain Buggy! Be careful!

298
00:23:11,010 --> 00:23:13,150
He has devil fruit powers too!

299
00:23:13,150 --> 00:23:15,250
He's a rubber person!

300
00:23:15,250 --> 00:23:16,040
What?!

301
00:23:16,040 --> 00:23:17,520
Rubber person?!

302
00:23:17,520 --> 00:23:19,830
Yeah! See!

303
00:23:20,290 --> 00:23:22,030
A devil fruit...

304
00:23:22,030 --> 00:23:25,530
That explains how he
bounced back the Buggy Ball.

305
00:23:28,760 --> 00:23:34,430
Cabaji "the Acrobat"
(Second) First Mate, Buggy Pirates

306
00:23:29,230 --> 00:23:32,240
This is the greatest insult
since we hoisted our flag.

307
00:23:33,480 --> 00:23:34,430
Captain.

308
00:23:34,430 --> 00:23:39,410
Oh, Cabaji! I'm so angry
I'm seeing red.

309
00:23:39,410 --> 00:23:42,850
Cabaji! What the hell
did you do to Richie?!

310
00:23:42,850 --> 00:23:44,150
This cat?

311
00:23:44,150 --> 00:23:47,580
I used it to shield me
so I wouldn't get my clothes dirty.

312
00:23:49,550 --> 00:23:50,360
Richie!

313
00:23:52,640 --> 00:23:55,830
Hey, Richie! Say something!
Are you all right?!

314
00:24:00,230 --> 00:24:01,710
Richie!

315
00:24:01,710 --> 00:24:04,480
Dammit, you bastard!

316
00:24:06,710 --> 00:24:07,840
Out of the way!

317
00:24:08,420 --> 00:24:10,550
No, you get outta my way!

318
00:24:15,470 --> 00:24:17,040
Captain Buggy.

319
00:24:17,760 --> 00:24:19,280
Yes, Cabaji?

320
00:24:19,710 --> 00:24:21,940
Please leave this to me.

321
00:24:21,940 --> 00:24:23,150
Sounds good!

322
00:24:23,150 --> 00:24:25,270
Go give 'em an acrobat show!

323
00:24:31,570 --> 00:24:34,240
I, First Mate Cabaji the Acrobat,

324
00:24:34,240 --> 00:24:39,040
will manifest
Captain Buggy's displeasure!

325
00:24:40,820 --> 00:24:43,420
I'll clash swords with you.

326
00:24:44,020 --> 00:24:46,700
Quite the honor, Roronoa Zoro.

327
00:24:47,760 --> 00:24:51,090
As a swordsman myself,
I am happy to cut you down.

328
00:24:53,590 --> 00:24:56,890
Hey, Zoro! You should
really rest! I'll handle this!

329
00:24:56,890 --> 00:24:59,100
Stay out of this!

330
00:24:59,100 --> 00:25:02,660
That's the stab wound
the captain gave him. What a fool.

331
00:25:03,360 --> 00:25:05,100
Acrobatics: Dire Fire!

332
00:25:15,170 --> 00:25:16,240
Something wrong?

333
00:25:16,240 --> 00:25:18,740
I swear I didn't kick you that hard.

334
00:25:19,250 --> 00:25:21,870
He fights dirty,
going after his injury like that!

335
00:25:23,980 --> 00:25:27,080
Acrobatics: Steamy Hot Spring Murder Mystery!

336
00:25:30,650 --> 00:25:32,270
Acrobatics, my ass!

337
00:25:32,270 --> 00:25:34,010
That's just kicking up dust!

338
00:25:40,050 --> 00:25:41,100
He did it again!

339
00:25:42,880 --> 00:25:47,060
What's wrong? A grown man
wailing is disgraceful!

340
00:25:47,650 --> 00:25:50,650
Well? Now do you see
how foolish it was

341
00:25:50,650 --> 00:25:54,940
to make an enemy
of the Buggy Pirates?

342
00:25:57,780 --> 00:26:00,930
As hurt as he is,
it's a miracle he's still alive!

343
00:26:01,760 --> 00:26:03,900
Why are you just
standing there watching?!

344
00:26:03,900 --> 00:26:05,160
He's gonna get killed!

345
00:26:12,880 --> 00:26:14,810
Roronoa Zoro...

346
00:26:14,810 --> 00:26:15,840
accept defeat!

347
00:26:17,050 --> 00:26:19,010
Annoying bastard!

348
00:26:21,060 --> 00:26:23,310
Is poking my wound...

349
00:26:23,310 --> 00:26:25,600
that much fun?!

350
00:26:28,520 --> 00:26:29,400
Ow!

351
00:26:35,080 --> 00:26:36,610
Wh-Why didn't you dodge that?!

352
00:26:37,480 --> 00:26:40,980
Is that enough
of a handicap for you?

353
00:26:42,190 --> 00:26:46,910
Now I'll show you...
just how outclassed you are!

354
00:26:49,070 --> 00:26:50,040
So cool!

355
00:26:51,350 --> 00:26:53,470
So this is Roronoa Zoro, huh?

356
00:26:54,030 --> 00:26:55,340
You think you can mock me...

357
00:26:55,860 --> 00:26:58,610
It's my dream to be
the world's greatest swordsman.

358
00:26:59,250 --> 00:27:04,360
I can't lose even once to anyone
who's considered a swordsman!

359
00:27:04,360 --> 00:27:05,310
I see...

360
00:27:06,500 --> 00:27:08,900
A strong resolve keeps you going.

361
00:27:09,890 --> 00:27:11,860
But never fear.

362
00:27:12,470 --> 00:27:15,820
Wounds as bad as yours will
make an excellent excuse...

363
00:27:16,360 --> 00:27:18,910
to explain why you lost to me!

364
00:27:18,910 --> 00:27:20,780
To hell with that...

365
00:27:21,480 --> 00:27:25,640
If I lose to someone like you
with such light injuries,

366
00:27:26,360 --> 00:27:28,920
then my future isn't looking too bright!

367
00:27:30,630 --> 00:27:32,460
Why, you...!

368
00:27:32,460 --> 00:27:34,490
Do it, Zoro!

369
00:27:36,320 --> 00:27:38,060
This is too much for me.

370
00:27:38,060 --> 00:27:41,430
You pirates go and injure
yourselves all you want.

371
00:27:42,300 --> 00:27:46,600
Besides, I have no stake
in whether you win or lose.

372
00:27:47,350 --> 00:27:50,940
Now's a good chance for me to swipe
the treasure and make tracks.

373
00:27:52,810 --> 00:27:55,190
Let's team up again
if we ever get the chance!

374
00:27:55,740 --> 00:27:57,860
See ya! Good luck with the fight!

375
00:27:57,860 --> 00:27:59,650
Yeah! Thanks!

376
00:28:00,190 --> 00:28:02,910
Taste my ultimate acrobatic move!

377
00:28:06,960 --> 00:28:10,370
Acrobatics:
100 Whirling Kamikaze Dervishes!

378
00:28:15,660 --> 00:28:18,920
Acrobatics: Alpine Ascent!

379
00:28:19,910 --> 00:28:23,050
Acrobatics:
Midsummer Fireworks!

380
00:28:23,050 --> 00:28:25,050
Whoa, he's soaring!

381
00:28:25,050 --> 00:28:27,390
Unicycle Thorn!

382
00:28:28,420 --> 00:28:31,520
Ground-hugging
Part-Part Cannon!

383
00:28:33,940 --> 00:28:37,650
Cabaji! I'll hold Zoro down!
Finish him off!

384
00:28:38,100 --> 00:28:39,110
As you wish!

385
00:28:40,680 --> 00:28:42,950
You bastards!

386
00:28:48,850 --> 00:28:49,540
Luffy!

387
00:28:51,200 --> 00:28:52,210
Curse you!

388
00:28:53,080 --> 00:28:54,810
Zoro's fight...

389
00:28:55,590 --> 00:28:56,860
is off limits.

390
00:29:01,140 --> 00:29:05,360
I can defeat you easily enough
without my captain's help!

391
00:29:05,360 --> 00:29:08,120
Enough... I'm tired...

392
00:29:10,940 --> 00:29:12,930
Finally given up, have you?

393
00:29:14,120 --> 00:29:18,190
Though I must say, I'm impressed
you could fight with such injuries.

394
00:29:19,900 --> 00:29:25,240
I meant I'm tired...
of your crappy-ass acrobatics!

395
00:29:27,050 --> 00:29:30,580
Then I'll finish you off... with my...

396
00:29:32,090 --> 00:29:34,000
real swordsmanship!

397
00:29:35,790 --> 00:29:37,000
Die!

398
00:29:39,150 --> 00:29:39,920
Oni...

399
00:29:40,560 --> 00:29:41,460
Giri!

400
00:29:45,970 --> 00:29:47,010
Cabaji!

401
00:29:49,640 --> 00:29:51,450
We, the Buggy Pirates...

402
00:29:51,970 --> 00:29:53,950
beaten by pesky thieves!

403
00:29:58,180 --> 00:30:00,010
"Thieves"? Nah...

404
00:30:03,600 --> 00:30:05,080
We're pirates!

405
00:30:07,160 --> 00:30:09,650
Luffy! I'm gonna sleep now!

406
00:30:09,650 --> 00:30:12,540
Right! I'll handle the rest!

407
00:30:17,640 --> 00:30:20,320
You guys are pirates?!

408
00:30:20,320 --> 00:30:23,370
Yeah! We're headed
for the Grand Line!

409
00:30:24,410 --> 00:30:29,720
Half-baked nobodies like you can't
handle that kind of voyage, dimwit!

410
00:30:30,180 --> 00:30:33,420
What are you gonna do
in the Grand Line, anyway?!

411
00:30:33,930 --> 00:30:36,350
Go on a sightseeing trip
or something?

412
00:30:40,480 --> 00:30:41,810
Become King of the Pirates!

413
00:30:43,230 --> 00:30:45,530
Get real, you flashy fool!

414
00:30:45,530 --> 00:30:47,450
If you're King of the Pirates,

415
00:30:47,450 --> 00:30:49,490
does that make me
God of the Pirates?!

416
00:30:49,490 --> 00:30:53,670
I'll be King of the Pirates
and obtain the world's treasures!

417
00:30:53,670 --> 00:30:55,640
You're dreaming!

418
00:30:55,640 --> 00:30:57,160
You're annoying.

419
00:30:57,900 --> 00:30:59,920
Just bring it on already!

420
00:31:02,490 --> 00:31:06,800
That straw hat of yours
reminds me of a certain man,

421
00:31:06,800 --> 00:31:09,130
and it bugs me!

422
00:31:09,660 --> 00:31:14,350
It reminds me of that dog...
of that red-haired bastard!

423
00:31:15,020 --> 00:31:15,810
"Red-haired"?!

424
00:31:16,450 --> 00:31:20,380
You said "red-haired"!
Does that mean you know Shanks?!

425
00:31:20,380 --> 00:31:23,620
Huh? Yeah, but what's it to you?

426
00:31:23,620 --> 00:31:24,980
Do you... know where he is?!

427
00:31:24,980 --> 00:31:27,780
Who can say?!
I might know where he is,

428
00:31:27,780 --> 00:31:30,150
but, then again, maybe I don't!

429
00:31:31,480 --> 00:31:33,870
That makes no sense.
Are you an idiot?

430
00:31:33,870 --> 00:31:35,450
Look who's talking!

431
00:31:36,270 --> 00:31:41,670
I'm not nice enough of a guy to just
tell you what you wanna know!

432
00:31:42,140 --> 00:31:44,290
Then I'll make you tell me!

433
00:31:46,150 --> 00:31:49,010
I'll kill you before that ever happens!

434
00:31:49,820 --> 00:31:52,340
I doubt rubber can
bounce back blades...

435
00:31:52,820 --> 00:31:53,800
Nope, it can't!

436
00:31:57,470 --> 00:31:59,890
Part-Part Slicecracker!

437
00:32:02,560 --> 00:32:07,320
Can't move in midair, can you?!

438
00:32:08,150 --> 00:32:09,400
Can too!

439
00:32:13,920 --> 00:32:16,990
Oh, my! Quite interesting!

440
00:32:17,830 --> 00:32:19,090
Same to you!

441
00:32:19,090 --> 00:32:21,370
Gum-Gum Pistol!

442
00:32:22,940 --> 00:32:24,580
Your moves are creative,

443
00:32:24,580 --> 00:32:26,920
but they leave you wide open!

444
00:32:27,630 --> 00:32:29,010
Time to carve you up!

445
00:32:29,010 --> 00:32:30,630
Gum-Gum...

446
00:32:30,630 --> 00:32:32,340
Part-Part Quick Escape!

447
00:32:32,720 --> 00:32:34,640
Sickle!

448
00:32:40,760 --> 00:32:41,980
Not good enough, "Gum-Gum"!

449
00:32:47,640 --> 00:32:50,360
Damn, you keep coming apart!

450
00:32:50,840 --> 00:32:55,490
Wh-What a fight.
It's like something out of a dream.

451
00:32:56,070 --> 00:32:58,490
H-Hey... You see that?

452
00:32:58,490 --> 00:33:01,700
You dumbass! Keep pretending
to be knocked out!

453
00:33:01,700 --> 00:33:06,460
Get caught up in that, and you'd
never have enough lives to survive!

454
00:33:06,460 --> 00:33:08,420
Part-Part Cannon!

455
00:33:10,840 --> 00:33:12,420
Separate!

456
00:33:16,940 --> 00:33:19,670
Well?! Do you see now, short stuff?!

457
00:33:28,390 --> 00:33:29,320
You bastard!

458
00:33:29,780 --> 00:33:33,780
Oh? Can't handle
a little scratch to your face?

459
00:33:34,840 --> 00:33:35,590
How dare you...

460
00:33:36,170 --> 00:33:39,740
How dare you damage this hat!

461
00:33:40,180 --> 00:33:40,990
Huh?

462
00:33:41,290 --> 00:33:43,350
This is my treasure!

463
00:33:43,350 --> 00:33:46,420
No one damages this hat
and gets away with it!

464
00:33:48,170 --> 00:33:52,440
Yeah. I swore to the person
who gave me this straw hat

465
00:33:52,440 --> 00:33:54,840
that I'd gather a crew
and become a pirate!

466
00:33:55,680 --> 00:33:59,300
I thought there was nothing
that could faze him...

467
00:34:00,210 --> 00:34:03,970
but he looks pretty upset.

468
00:34:06,940 --> 00:34:10,450
It would seem that hat
has a history to it.

469
00:34:11,000 --> 00:34:11,790
That's right!

470
00:34:12,660 --> 00:34:14,550
Is it that important of a hat?

471
00:34:20,700 --> 00:34:22,330
If so...

472
00:34:22,330 --> 00:34:23,580
then protect it better!

473
00:34:40,250 --> 00:34:42,010
I'll leave this hat with you.

474
00:34:42,810 --> 00:34:44,600
It's dear to me.

475
00:34:45,130 --> 00:34:46,310
Take good care of it!

476
00:34:53,760 --> 00:34:56,610
Come bring it back to me someday...

477
00:34:58,910 --> 00:35:00,800
once you've become a great pirate!

478
00:35:02,210 --> 00:35:04,720
That's our promise... Luffy!

479
00:35:14,630 --> 00:35:18,170
You call this filthy
straw hat a treasure?

480
00:35:18,170 --> 00:35:19,760
Cut the crap!

481
00:35:22,280 --> 00:35:25,470
Shanks and I made
a promise on that hat!

482
00:35:25,470 --> 00:35:26,350
What?!

483
00:35:27,060 --> 00:35:29,990
Meaning this is Shanks' hat?!

484
00:35:30,600 --> 00:35:32,360
No wonder it seemed familiar!

485
00:35:33,190 --> 00:35:35,820
He always wore this around me!

486
00:35:37,000 --> 00:35:39,400
You and Shanks
sailed aboard the same ship?!

487
00:35:39,400 --> 00:35:43,190
Oh, yeah, back during
our pirate apprenticeships.

488
00:35:43,190 --> 00:35:44,910
We were shipmates...

489
00:35:45,660 --> 00:35:48,830
me and that damn, detestable,
red-haired bastard!

490
00:35:50,920 --> 00:35:53,380
Shanks is a great man!

491
00:35:53,730 --> 00:35:55,040
You, his shipmate?!

492
00:35:55,040 --> 00:35:58,010
Don't compare yourself to him!

493
00:35:58,500 --> 00:36:00,800
Part-Part Quick Escape!

494
00:36:02,680 --> 00:36:03,990
Hi, I'm Buggy!

495
00:36:06,500 --> 00:36:09,850
Never say you and Shanks
were shipmates ever again!

496
00:36:13,460 --> 00:36:16,190
I can say whatever
I want about Shanks!

497
00:36:19,850 --> 00:36:23,360
Tell me! What happened
between you and Shanks?!

498
00:36:24,820 --> 00:36:28,310
Damn! You actually
ripped up my treasure!

499
00:36:31,290 --> 00:36:33,250
Wanna know that badly?

500
00:36:34,100 --> 00:36:39,760
He's the one person...
I absolutely cannot forgive!

501
00:36:40,500 --> 00:36:43,460
I'll curse him
for the rest of my life!

502
00:36:44,330 --> 00:36:47,250
I'll never forgive him!
